   I have prepared a DOS shell script (MAKEPAGE.BAT) and a MAWK script
   which together will perform a simple search and produce a HTML page
   based on the results, i.e.

       makepage mlatu

   produces RES.HTM which is viewable with any Web client. Due to limitations
   of the DOS version of mawk, the operation is performed in two steps:
   the first step prepares a MAWK script which is used to perform the search
   at the second step (also, I am no AWK wizard :-(

   I have put a copy of the dictionary (GISMU.DCT, which contains preformatted
   <dt> ... <dd> lines) and the scripts as a zip archive (gdict.zip) to

      ftp://xiron.pc.helsinki.fi/pub/lojban/gdict.zip

   A DOS executable for mawk is also available there at

      ftp://xiron.pc.helsinki.fi/pub/lojban/mawk.zip

   The preformatted dictionary can, of course, be used with any search
   mechanism to produce a Web page.

